From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Michael Pfeifroth <micpf@westermo.com>
Date: Mon, 22 Jun 2026 14:13:37 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] wifi-scripts: enforce WPA3 for all encryption types on 6 GHz

The existing 6 GHz auth_type override only covers mixed modes
(psk-sae, eap-eap2), upgrading them to their WPA3 equivalents.
However, if a user configures pure WPA2 (psk or eap) on a 6 GHz
radio, the configuration falls through unchanged and hostapd rejects
it with a confusing error about invalid AKM suite.

Extend the override to also cover pure WPA2 modes:
  - psk / psk-sae -> sae
  - eap / eap-eap2 -> eap2

This matches the existing silent-upgrade pattern and ensures the
radio comes up regardless of which legacy encryption the user
selected.

Signed-off-by: Michael Pfeifroth <micpf@westermo.com>
Link: https://github.com/openwrt/openwrt/pull/23914
[Crescentm: from OpenWrt PR #23914 head eb7da521371a605960575e6cdfcbdb81f7a4c4e9,
 without its Makefile PKG_RELEASE bump. Also set wpa=2 on 6 GHz: the
 encryption values psk, psk+*, psk-mixed, wpa and wpa-mixed leave wpa at
 1 or 3, hostapd then refuses the BSS ("Pre-RSNA security methods are
 not allowed in 6 GHz"), and iface_mfp() sets up no PMF for wpa < 2.
 This replaces the earlier local 952, which did the same upgrade with
 its own code; its file name is kept. Also drop TKIP from wpa_pairwise
 on 6 GHz (falling back to CCMP if nothing is left): the tkip and
 tkip+ccmp suffixes (e.g. psk2+tkip, psk-mixed+tkip+ccmp, wpa2+tkip)
 otherwise make hostapd refuse the BSS, as TKIP is not allowed there.]
---
 files-ucode/usr/share/ucode/wifi/ap.uc | 18 ++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/files-ucode/usr/share/ucode/wifi/ap.uc b/files-ucode/usr/share/ucode/wifi/ap.uc
index 51e2fe1..085a3f2 100644
--- a/files-ucode/usr/share/ucode/wifi/ap.uc
+++ b/files-ucode/usr/share/ucode/wifi/ap.uc
@@ -568,10 +568,24 @@ export function generate(interface, data, config, vlans, stas, phy_features) {
 
 	iface.parse_encryption(config, data.config, phy_features);
 	if (data.config.band == '6g') {
-		if (config.auth_type == 'psk-sae')
+		if (config.auth_type in ['psk', 'psk-sae'])
 			config.auth_type = 'sae';
-		if (config.auth_type == 'eap-eap2')
+		if (config.auth_type in ['eap', 'eap-eap2'])
 			config.auth_type = 'eap2';
+		/*
+		 * 6 GHz allows RSN only, and PMF is only set up for wpa >= 2:
+		 * WPA and WPA/WPA2 mixed encryption values leave wpa at 1 or 3.
+		 */
+		if (config.wpa)
+			config.wpa = 2;
+		/*
+		 * TKIP is not allowed on 6 GHz either: drop it from the
+		 * pairwise ciphers of the tkip and tkip+ccmp suffixes.
+		 */
+		if (config.wpa_pairwise) {
+			let pairwise = filter(split(config.wpa_pairwise, ' '), c => c != 'TKIP');
+			config.wpa_pairwise = length(pairwise) ? join(' ', pairwise) : 'CCMP';
+		}
 	}
 
 	if (config.auth_type in [ 'psk', 'psk-sae', 'psk-sae-compat' ] && data.config.band != '6g')
